## 3. Mutation bounds and rollback

| Write class | Bound | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| Forward worker script uploads | **exactly 1** | 31 parts, byte-identical to the stamped manifest (§1.3) |
| Observability PATCH after forward upload | **≤1, conditional** | ONLY if the post-upload read shows observability reset (§4) |
| Rollback uploads | **≤1, conditional** | ONLY for a **class A** confirmed deployment defect (§3.1), after the §3.2 safety conditions verify; the byte-identical preserved live parts (§1.3 item 6). **Class B findings never fire a rollback inside this gate** |
| Observability PATCH after rollback | **≤1, conditional** | Same condition, after a class A rollback upload |
| Containment transitions | **0** | No `contain_drive`, no `stop_chain`, no `clear`, no `verify_chain_stop` |
| Commands / reports / SubmitJob | **0** | — |
| Hold flips / settings flips / queue changes | **0** | GENERATION_HALT stays `"1"`; queue stays paused |
| Alarm registrations caused by this gate | **0 expected** | A deploy is not a wake; any `armedAt` change is a finding to classify (trigger T6), not a budget item |
| Recorder rows | **0 expected** | The recorder writes only from the alarm handler |
| Spend | **$0** | No dispatch is possible under the holds; dispatched must remain 0 (§5, V7) |

**Rollback triggers (named). Every trigger STOPs the
gate. What follows the STOP is decided by the
trigger's class (§3.1) — no trigger causes a rollback
automatically.**

- **T1** — post-upload read-back parts not
  byte-identical to the stamped manifest. **[Class A]**
- **T2** — `/health` build stamp ≠ the build pin, or
  generation not `halted`, or coordinator not `armed`.
  **[Class A]**
- **T3** — settings/bindings regression: settings
  revision ≠ 1, bindings ≠ 10, GENERATION_HALT ≠ `"1"`,
  phase policy ≠ `enforce`, or observability not
  restorable within the §4 budget. **[Class A]**
- **T4** — containment surface misbehavior: the state
  route or the `drive=1` containment projection errors,
  reports any state other than NORMAL, reports
  `verified: false` against an absent store, or
  `stopConfidence` ≠ `"not_applicable"` at rest.
  **[Class A]**
- **T5** — any §5 preservation item fails: a change vs
  census in the preserved plan, its job, the exemption
  projection, the parked job, the conflicts baseline,
  any phase figure, quota, or the watermarks that is
  not fully explained by the deploy itself (the deploy
  explains ONLY the script etag and build stamp
  changing). **[Class B]**
- **T6** — `armedAt` changed across the upload
  (unexplained alarm-registration movement).
  **[Class B]**

### 3.1 Finding classification and permitted responses

Every post-upload finding is classified before any
response beyond the STOP. The classification — not the
executor — decides what may happen next.

- **Class A — CONFIRMED DEPLOYMENT DEFECT.** The
  evidence ties the finding to the uploaded code or to
  the upload itself. Qualifying evidence: the finding
  sits on a surface the uploaded script owns (script
  parts / etag, the build stamp, the settings/bindings
  projection, the new containment surfaces); OR an
  error reproduces on the new build that the §2 census
  showed absent on the old build; OR a post-upload
  read-back mismatches the stamped manifest. T1–T4 are
  class A by construction. **Permitted response:**
  rollback inside this gate's §3 budget — at most one
  rollback upload plus at most one conditional
  observability PATCH — once **every** §3.2 safety
  condition is verified. Nothing else beyond the
  rollback sequence and HOLD is authorized.
- **Class B — EXTERNAL OR CAUSALLY UNRESOLVED
  MOVEMENT.** Movement with no established causal link
  to the deploy. Two families: (i) movement in surfaces
  a script upload cannot mechanically cause — a script
  upload invokes no DO method and writes none of the
  plan / job / exemption / quota / conflicts /
  watermark stores (T5), and it is not a wake and
  cannot mechanically re-register an alarm (T6); (ii)
  ANY finding, under any trigger, whose cause is
  undetermined after the evidence is captured.
  **Permitted response — the only one authorized: STOP,
  HOLD, preserve the evidence exactly as read, and
  escalate to Rowan and Julie.** A rollback for a
  class B finding is **NOT** inside this gate's budget
  and **NOT** authorized by this gate's GO; it requires
  a separate Rowan ruling and a separate Julie GO.
  Rolling back unexplained movement could destroy the
  evidence of what moved and could strand state written
  against either build — so the gate holds instead.
- **Doubt resolves to class B.** A finding is class A
  only when the executor can affirmatively tie it to
  the uploaded code with qualifying evidence. The
  executor's own tracing never promotes a finding to
  class A, and an ambiguous or partially explained
  finding stays class B until Rowan rules.

